<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7869" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδῐχα</span></b> , Adv., (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνά, δίχα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>asunder, in twain,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ δ᾽ [κεφαλὴ] ἄνδιχα πᾶσα κεάσθη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.412
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄνδιχα πάντα δάσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.511
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμμίγδην,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				912
			</span></i>; <i>far away,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.31
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as Prep., c.
			gen., <i>apart from,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.908
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.927
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλήλων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.4
				</span></i>
			 (Stat. Flacc.):—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδιχάζω</span></b> , <i>to be divided in
			opinion,</i> of judges, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(1).333
			</span></i> (
				Locr.
			).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
